finish
/clear
/uis,msgpop,2  ! this command and KEYW,PR_SGUI,1 are issued only so that
               ! the warning message is displayed at the end of execution

/prep7
et,1,188             ! geometry and mesh attributes don't seem to matter,
et,2,181             ! all that is needed for the bug to manifest seems
mp,ex,1,2e11         ! to be the presence of both SHELL elements (to which
mp,prxy,1,0.3        ! a pressure is applied with SFE) and BEAM elements
sectype,1,beam,rect  ! (to which a pressure is applied with SFBEAM). The
secdata,0.2,0.2      ! order in which these elements are created matters,
sectype,2,shell      ! as discussed below. When the right (or should it be
secdata,0.05         ! wrong?) conditions are met, the load step file written
k,1,0,0              ! with LSWRITE cannot be read by LSREAD. The lines
k,2,1,0              ! corresponding to the SFBEAM command seem to not have
k,3,1,1              ! the expected formatting and the read operation fails
k,4,0,1              ! with the 'not a recognized command' warning message.
a,1,2,3,4

aatt,1,,2,,2    ! meshing areas before lines is required for this bug to manifest
aesize,all,0.5  ! since the lower number elements appear first in the load step
amesh,all       ! listing, making the lines corresponding to SFEBLOCK command
                ! appear before those corresponding to SFBEAM command.

latt,1,,1,,,,1  ! if this code block meshing lines is moved above the one meshing
lesize,all,0.5  ! areas the bug no longer happens.
lmesh,all

dk,all,ux,0,,,uy,uz
esel,s,ename,,188
sfbeam,all,1,pres,404  ! the way SFBEAM command is transcribed to the load step
esel,s,ename,,181      ! file is what actually causes the LSREAD error. Note that
sfe,all,1,pres,,-941   ! the pressure value set here (404) is the one that appears
allsel                 ! in the warning message.
lswrite,1

/solu           ! here LSSOLVE fails because it issues LSREAD internally, which reads
antype,0        ! the (badly formatted?) .s01 load step file. The process is then
keyw,pr_sgui,1  ! interrupted and solution is not performed. The same '404 is not a
lssolve,1,1,1   ! recognized SOLUTION command' error can be reproduced simply by
                ! issuing LSREAD,1
